        "title": "refactor(agents): trim embedded runner exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe production-mode Knip baseline still carried 22 unused exports around the embedded agent runner facade, attempt helpers, run state, and context guard.\n\nRelated: #105595\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Remove redundant embedded-runner and attempt re-exports.\n- Point tests at the canonical owning modules instead of keeping facade aliases alive for tests.\n- Delete the now-test-only stream-resolution cache reset; the test already uses a fresh session object.\n- Make the preemptive overflow message private and keep the exact behavior assertion local to the test.\n- Regenerate against current main. Concurrent drift added ten newly exposed baseline entries and dropped four stale entries; the resulting baseline remains shrink-only at 16 fewer entries globally and under `src/agents`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone. Internal export-surface cleanup only; embedded run behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update`: regenerated to 5,511 entries.\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports`: passed at the pushed head.\n- `src/agents` baseline: 509 -> 493 entries after concurrent drift; all 22 intended entries are removed.\n- Focused remote Vitest proof: 201 tests passed across unit-fast (4), agents (179), and e2e (22) shards.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` and `pnpm tsgo:core:test`: passed.\n- Earlier broad `pnpm check:changed`: formatting, API/export guards, core and core-test typechecks, and the touched `src/agents` lint shard passed; Testbox later exited 137 in the unrelated `src/daemon` lint shard.\n- Fresh autoreview: one false positive rejected after checking the rebased source and passing both core typechecks; stream resolver calls now live in `run/attempt-stream-transport.ts`.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nNo changelog: internal dead-export cleanup only.\n",
